<title>UK: Macfarlane buys Alport for 9.1 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Macfarlane buys Alport for 9.1 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Macfarlane Group (Clansman) Plc, the Scottish-based packaging company, announced the acquisition of Alport Holdings for 9.1 million stg on Monday.</p>
<p>Alport makes polythene film in a factory based in Yorkshire, north of England. In the year ended April 30 Alport's pretax profits were 644.3 million stg, with net assets valued at 2.65 million.</p>
<p>The deal is seen bringing benefits through synergy and providing fresh scope for expansion, Macfarlane said.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
